            <ArticleTitle>Atypical heel pain. Hyperparathyroidism-induced stress fracture of the calcaneus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case of atypical heel pain masquerading as plantar fasciitis. The patient was subsequently diagnosed with hyperparathyroidism-induced stress fracture of the calcaneus. The clinical entity of hyperparathyroidism and its manifestations in the skeletal system are presented, as well as a review of stress fractures and pertinent imaging studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
